{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c011",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The reservation of \"any limitations defenses which may exist immediately before this agreement is executed\" pulls against the tolling promise in the preceding sentence, and no execution date is fixed anywhere in the letter (the letterhead says April 30, 2008 while the Memorandum of Understanding calls it the April 28, 2008 letter agreement). A court would have to decide as of what date the preserved defenses are measured.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.27}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"During the pendency of the Lawsuit\" is undefined, and the provision does not say whether pendency ends on a dismissal without prejudice or only on final resolution including appeals, as the tolling sentence two lines earlier phrases it. It also prescribes no consequence for a suit filed in breach of the bar.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.36},
     {"issue": "The flat prohibition on filing conflicts with the permission granted earlier in the same paragraph that \"U.S. Auto may, in a separate lawsuit, assert\" the Excess Funds Claim(s). The two must be reconciled to determine whether the right is granted or merely deferred.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c013",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "Defendants' concession that the Other Causes of Action do not share a nucleus of operative facts with the Lawsuit is hard to square with the definition of those causes of action, which concerns handling, reserves and closing of claims on the very reinsured policies at issue in the retained claims. Whether the parties can contract around the factual overlap is left to construction.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.21}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c014",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The express waiver of res judicata and collateral estoppel as to the Other Causes of Action conflicts with the closing paragraph, in which all parties \"reserve the right to contest any later-filed separate lawsuits, and may assert any and all applicable defenses or affirmative defenses.\" The instrument does not say which prevails.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c015",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "This tolling of the Other Causes of Action \"until the Lawsuit has been settled or otherwise finally resolved\" cannot be squared with Section VI of the Memorandum of Understanding, which tolls the same \"Other Causes of Action\" for five years or until all claims on the subject policies are paid and settled. The two agreements fix different tolling end points for identical claims.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33},
     {"issue": "\"Settled or otherwise finally resolved, including the completion of any appeals\" gives no answer for a dismissal without prejudice, which neither settles nor finally resolves the Lawsuit yet ends it. The end date of the toll is therefore indeterminate.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c016",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "Defendants' reservation of \"any limitations defenses which may exist immediately before this agreement is executed\" is in tension with their tolling promise in the preceding sentence, and the agreement fixes no execution date against which pre-existing defenses can be measured. Whether limitations that had partly run are preserved or suspended is unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c017",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The qualifier \"by entering into this agreement, in general\" is vague: it is unclear whether \"in general\" limits the non-concession to some acts and not others, or is mere surplusage. The scope of what Defendants are declining to concede therefore has no fixed boundary.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c018",
   "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c019",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The provision uses \"Excess Fund Claim(s)\" whereas the term defined earlier in the letter is \"the Excess Funds Claim(s),\" a mechanical mismatch in the defined term. It is a small point, but it leaves the referent of this sentence technically undefined.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.10}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c020",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The blanket reservation of \"any and all applicable defenses or affirmative defenses\" cannot be squared with the two earlier paragraphs in which Lincoln General and Defendants expressly relinquish and waive res judicata and collateral estoppel as to the Excess Funds Claim(s) and Other Causes of Action. Whether \"applicable\" silently excludes the waived preclusion defenses is precisely what would be argued.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.38}
   ]}
]}

